# Files the CI coding agent must never edit.
#
# On a public repo anyone can open an issue, and the issue body becomes the
# agent's prompt. An owner applying `ai_fix_it` is vouching for intent, not
# sanitizing content -- so a crafted issue could try to talk the agent into
# rewriting its own guardrails or leaking a key into a commit.
#
# CODEOWNERS already means none of this could MERGE without an owner
# approving, but keeping it out of the diff entirely makes those PRs
# reviewable instead of alarming.

# CI config, including the agent's own workflows and the CODEOWNERS file.
.github/

# Deployment config and anything that holds credentials.
deployment/
*.hjson
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
